RF.put("questb:b32",{"8592":{"id":8592,"t":"Tiara of the Oracle","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Vek'nilash's Circlet, 2 Idols of the Sage, 5 Silver Scarabs and 5 Bone Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Friendly reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nVek'nilash's Circlet Emperor Vek'nilash in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of the Sage Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Silver Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Bone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 3000 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"The Twin Emperors... their incessant whispers are slowly taking a toll on my sanity. They mock me, knowing I cannot step further into their domain to save my brother Arygos.\nIn my visions I see their monstrous faces adorned by powerful crowns. But I will have my revenge... I will transmute these symbols of Qiraji power to ones better suited to our needs.\nBring me the components I require, ‹name›. I will give you a headpiece of unmatched power.","rew":"You will receive:\nTiara of the Oracle\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Did you bring me the components I asked for, ‹name›?","done":"You've succeeded! The whispers from the Twin Emperors have ceased.\nTake this as a reward. The mere sight of it will strike fear in the hearts of the Qiraji... it shall remind them of their fallen leaders and of the mortal that slew them.\nStart Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Class Priest Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8592\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 16,550 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Tiara of the Oracle this quest\nBring Vek'nilash's Circlet, 2 Idols of the Sage, 5 Silver Scarabs and 5 Bone Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj.\nAndorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n9,950 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8512":{"id":8512,"t":"The Alliance Needs Light Leather!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from The Alliance Needs Light Leather!.","obj":"Bring 10 light leather to Bonnie Stoneflayer at the airfield in Dun Morogh.\n10 Light Leather Tattered Chest 18 % , Battered Chest 18 % , Armor Crate 0 % , Tattered Chest 0 % and 4 more","desc":"Good to see you again ‹name›. It does appear that we need more light leather for the creation of the various war materiel. If you could bring me a stack of ten that would be just perfect.","rew":"You will receive:\nAlliance Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"Good to see you again, ‹name›. It does appear that we need more light leather for the creation of the various war materiels. If you would bring me a stack of ten, that would be just perfect.","done":"Thank you for your generous donation, ‹name›. I'm going to get those onto the pile right now, and in no time I'm sure that they'll get changed into a nice set of armor, some leather patches, or used for something else in our preparations. Seems like we're always in need of more light leather. Come back and visit me soon.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":60.3,"y":33.4,"n":"Bonnie Stoneflayer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"92432":{"id":92432,"t":"An alarming request","lv":33,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Report to the Image of Archmage Modera near the City of Dalaran.","desc":"I bring ill tidings from Dalaran. Something has disrupted our ley lines, causing erratic and destructive behavior from our constructs in the city.\nWe know not yet what is causing this mayhem. The high council has ordered us to keep this matter private so as to not bring shame to our order. But we cannot keep up this charade forever. The city is being overrun as we speak!\nArchmage Modera has dispatched me to solicit outside aid. Seek her image out near Dalaran beside Lordamere Lake.\nHillsbrad Foothills Silverpine Forest","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":48.3,"y":60.1,"n":"Emissary Jacques","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":68.6,"y":45.2,"n":"Image of Archmage Modera","e":1}],"cats":["alterac-mountains"]},"512":{"id":512,"t":"Noble Deaths","lv":36,"min":26,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 7 Alterac Signet Rings to Magistrate Maleb in Southshore.\n7 Alterac Signet Ring Syndicate Wizard 80 % , Syndicate Enforcer 80 % , Syndicate Assassin 80 % , Syndicate Saboteur 80 % and 3 more","desc":"I fear the leadership behind the Syndicate is bent on Southshore's ruin. We must strike hard at these leaders before their plans are realized.\nEnter the ruins of Strahnbrad, in the Alterac Mountains to the north. We think the Syndicate is using the area as a headquarters.\nWe know this gang of cutthroats is run by former Alterac nobles. They may be hiding as normal Syndicate agents, but you'll know you've killed a noble by the signet ring he wears.\nBring me those signet rings.","rew":"Money: 40 0 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,800\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Have you been hunting the Syndicate? Do you have those rings?","done":"Stripping the Syndicate of its nobility will remove its ability to act decisively, and reduce it to nothing more than a gang of thugs.\nYou serve your Alliance well, ‹name›.\nHillsbrad Foothills Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":48.1,"y":59.1,"n":"Magistrate Henry Maleb","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alterac-mountains"]},"8272":{"id":8272,"t":"Hero of the Frostwolf","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBloodseeker Ice Barbed Spear Wand of Biting Cold Cold Forged Hammer\nExperience: 650\n+10 reputation with Frostwolf Clan\n+10 reputation with Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":63.8,"y":60.5,"n":"Voggah Deathgrip","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alterac-valley"]},"672":{"id":672,"t":"Raising Spirits","lv":34,"min":29,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Acquire 10 Highland Raptor Eyes from Highland Striders and Highland Thrashers for Tor'gan in Hammerfall.\n10 Highland Raptor Eye Highland Strider 33 % , Highland Thrasher 33 %","desc":"We tried to settle him in, cheer him up, telling him stories of our mighty city at Orgrimmar in Kalimdor, but nothing would move him.\nTales of our young Warchief, Thrall, who bears the armor and hammer of Orgrim... but, perhaps... Perhaps! A demonstration of our newly found shamanistic magic would give him new hope. It is worth a try!\nA small object we could make for him, yes... Bring me some raptor eyes, and I will see what I can do.","rew":"Experience: 2,700\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"I will create an amulet that will give Gor'mul some of the strength of the raptors. Perhaps that will awaken some flame within him...","done":"Excellent. The spirits of the raptors that gave these eyes will lend strength to the bearer of this amulet.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":74.7,"y":36.3,"n":"Tor'gan","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"2752":{"id":2752,"t":"On Iron Pauldrons","lv":32,"min":32,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring four Bronze Battleaxes and four Bronze Warhammers to Orokk Omosh in Orgrimmar.\n4 Bronze Battle Axe\n4 Bronze Warhammer","desc":"Orokk sees the eagerness in your eyes, ‹name›. Like a sponge you soak in the wisdom of the Omosh.\nThree lessons I shall teach!\nReturn to the anvil, soak in the heat of the forge, create for Orokk four bronze battleaxes and four bronze warhammers. Only then will you learn of the iron pauldron.","rew":"You will receive:\nPlans: Barbaric Iron Shoulders\nExperience: 2,550","back":"Show me your dedication, ‹race›.","done":"You do Orokk proud, ‹name›. Read, learn of iron shoulders!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":79.2,"y":22.4,"n":"Orokk Omosh","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"97952":{"id":97952,"t":"Camping 101 blacksmithing","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Basil Frye in Undercity to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your blacksmithing skill to 20","desc":"So, you've become a Blacksmith. That's a great choice if you want to make sure your blades never dull.\nI reckon I know someone that can help with that by teaching you how to craft a Sharpening Wheel. Bring one of these out at your camp and all the warriors and rogues in the area will be lining up to hone their weapons.","back":"Yes, I can teach you.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Sharpening Wheel. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.\nTirisfal Glades Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":57.2,"y":55.4,"n":"Eleanor Shackleton","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":60,"y":28.6,"n":"Basil Frye","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94272":{"id":94272,"t":"Craftsmans writ blue glittering axe","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Blue Glittering Axe\nBlue Glittering Axe","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Blue Glittering Axe, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Blue Glittering Axe Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94272","cats":["crafting"]},"94352":{"id":94352,"t":"Craftsmans writ wizardweave turban","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Wizardweave Turban\nWizardweave Turban","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Wizardweave Turban, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Wizardweave Turban Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94352","cats":["crafting"]},"7792":{"id":7792,"t":"A Donation of Wool","lv":60,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"60 Wool Cloth Farrin Daris 66.7 % , Adam Lind 62.1 % , Mountaineer Langarr 57.1 % , Protector Leick 47.6 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 650\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","back":"We are currently gathering wool. A donation of sixty pieces of wool cloth will net you full recognition by our people for your generous actions.\nIf you currently have sixty pieces, you may donate them now.","done":"Wonderful! We thank you for your generous donation, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":64,"y":23,"n":"Raedon Duskstriker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darnassus"]},"94912":{"id":94912,"t":"Child of nature","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Sheldras Moontree in Stormwind.","desc":"Greetings, young ‹class›.\nHave you heard of the Cenarion Circle? I'd expect not. They are an ancient order of naturalists and practitioners of the druidic arts, much like yourself. In the city of Stormwind you'll find a night elf by the name of Sheldras Moontree. He will teach you how to reach the stronghold of the Cenarion Circle on Kalimdor, a place called Moonglade.\nGo now. You have much to learn if you wish to save your home.","done":"Greetings, fellow ‹class›. It pleases me to meet a fellow ‹class› from among the Skyborne, and to be among the first to welcome you to Azeroth.\nI think you will find that my fellow druids of the Cenarion Circle have much wisdom to impart upon you, child of nature.\nAlterac Mountains Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":18.8,"y":78.6,"n":"Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver","s":1},{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":11.8,"y":56.6,"n":"Alfina Nightgaze","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":21,"y":55.4,"n":"Sheldras Moontree","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"272":{"id":272,"t":"Trial of the Sea Lion","lv":16,"min":16,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the Half Pendant of Aquatic Agility and the Half Pendant of Aquatic Endurance. Speak with the residents of Moonglade to learn clues as to where these items may be located.\nForm the Pendant of the Sea Lion from the two pendant halves. You need to be in proximity of the Shrine of Remulos to do this.\nBring the joined pendant to Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven, Moonglade.\nPendant of the Sea Lion","desc":"For the second trial, you'll need the two halves that make the Pendant of the Sea Lion. One half draws power from the agility of the sea lion aspect, gliding through water; the other draws power from the incredible endurance of the sea lion aspect. Druids draw on both these traits equally to embody the aspect of their aquatic form.\nSpeak with the locals of Moonglade to learn where the parts may lie, and bring both here to join them together. Once formed, take the pendant to Dendrite Starblaze.","rew":"Experience: 875\n+75 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Have you formed your pendant for me to inspect, ‹name›? If you need help in locating the parts, try asking the local populace for information. Not only will you find what you seek, but it will give you a reason to explore this wondrous and sacred glade.","done":"You've completed the Trial of the Sea Lion, ‹name› - congratulations.\nEach task in acquiring the pendant shows that both agility and endurance are necessary to act in harmony with what you desire to do underwater. Neither can exist without the other, and both cannot be done without your willingness to embrace the aspect of the sea lion.\nRemember these lessons well, and count on them once you have gained your aquatic form.\nMoonglade Darkshore Silverpine Forest","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":36.5,"y":40.1,"n":"Tajarri","s":1},{"z":"Moonglade","x":56.2,"y":30.6,"n":"Dendrite Starblaze","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"432":{"id":432,"t":"Those Blasted Troggs!","lv":9,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 6 Rockjaw Skullthumpers for Foreman Stonebrow at the Gol'Bolar quarry.\nRockjaw Skullthumper slain : 0/ 6","desc":"Those Light-blasted troggs, turning my work site into a wreck! Look at that, there goes another barrel of powder!\nOhhh, I wish I could go down there and wring every one of their scrawny little necks! I want to kill them all!\nThis can't be good for my health, all this stress and anger... What have they left me with? Nothing!\nI'd kill them myself, but my aim's no good anymore! You go into the quarry and kill some of the filthy buggers! I'll pay you! Just hurt them, kill them!","rew":"Money: 2 0 gold, 2 silver, 0 copper Experience: 600\n+75 reputation with Ironforge\n+75 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"It makes me so mad! Grrr...","done":"Well, that makes me feel a little better...\nBut I won't be happy until they're all dead! All of them!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":69.1,"y":56.3,"n":"Foreman Stonebrow","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"832":{"id":832,"t":"Burning Shadows","lv":12,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take this eye to Neeru Fireblade.\nEye of Burning Shadow Gazz'uz\nProvided: Eye of Burning Shadow","desc":"<Words emanate from the pendant and into your mind.>\nGazz'uz?\nGazz'uz...report!\nThere is word of your discovery in Skull Rock. You must prepare for an attack!\nGazz'uz, I order you to speak! Speak or I will make sure Neeru Fireblade knows of your presence, and he will descend on you with swift brutality.\nDo not test your skills against Neeru...\n...Gazz'uz, are you there...?","rew":"Experience: 675\n+75 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+75 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"You have something vital to report. I can sense it behind your eyes.","done":"<Examines the Eye of Burning Shadow>\nIntriguing. The voice you heard mentioned my name? I am known for hunting down enemies of our Warchief, but...it is strange that I was singled out. Stranger still that the Burning Blade cultists from whom you recovered this pendant have a name so close to my own.\nI must study this pendant. I must study and, and must ponder the meaning of its message.\nThank you for bringing this to my attention, ‹name›. You have done your people a great service.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":49.5,"y":50.6,"n":"Neeru Fireblade","e":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"5152":{"id":5152,"t":"Auntie Marlene","lv":56,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Marlene, south of the Ruins of Andorhal.","desc":"Oh, I'm so lonely! Where is my family? Auntie Marlene told me to stay here, but then she left and never came back! And my dad... have you seen him?\nMaybe Auntie Marlene knows where he is. She lives near Andorhal, in a house to the south. I think it was on a hill... she said it was on a hill.\nPlease, ‹name›. You're my new friend! Will you talk to my Auntie for me?","rew":"Experience: 2,900","done":"You saw Pamela? How is she? Is she alive?? Oh, no! Poor Pamela! She was so young, and such a happy child...\nShe doesn't know what happened to her father, does she? My brother, Joseph?\nNo... she couldn't understand what happened to Joseph. And even if she could, I don't have the heart to tell her...\nEastern Plaguelands Western Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":31.2,"y":78,"n":"Pamela Redpath","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":49.2,"y":78.6,"n":"Marlene Redpath","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"112":{"id":112,"t":"Collecting Kelp","lv":7,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 4 Crystal Kelp Fronds to William Pestle in Goldshire.\n4 Crystal Kelp Frond Murloc Streamrunner 33 % , Murloc 33 %","desc":"I can make an invisibility liquor for Maybell, so she can slip away from the Maclure Vineyards and go to Tommy Joe. But to make the Liquor, I need some crystal kelp.\nAlthough the kelp usually grows in the ocean... sometimes murlocs collect it. See if the murlocs near Crystal Lake have any. Crystal Lake is just east of Goldshire.","rew":"Experience: 320\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Do you have that crystal kelp? I'm sure Maybell is anxious to see her beau...","done":"You got them. Good show! Now, just one moment while I concoct the potion...","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":43.3,"y":65.7,"n":"William Pestle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"3632":{"id":3632,"t":"Gnome Engineering","lv":47,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"If you wish to learn more about Gnome Engineering, take the Manual of Engineering Disciplines to Tinkmaster Overspark in Ironforge.\nManual of Engineering Disciplines\nProvided: Manual of Engineering Disciplines","desc":"Engineering at the expert level breaks into two disciplines: gnome and goblin. Gnome engineering represents by far the superior of the two! It's about the construction of wonderful gadgets and devices that make life better!\n‹name›, read this manual. If you want to learn more on gnome engineering, then take that manual to Tinkmaster Overspark here in Ironforge. Remember - membership is permanent and prevents joining the other discipline, so make sure you are sure before finishing his task!","rew":"Experience: 420","back":"Yes, yes, what needs of yours might I address today? Clearly, I have the time to do such since all I do is stand here while our beloved city lies in a cloud of irradiated death.","done":"Ah, a young engineer interested in pursuing the one, true discipline of engineering! Well forgive my melodrama, friend. While our situation remains dire, it still is always a good day to see another engineer respond to the clarion call of true engineering!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.1,"y":28.1,"n":"Springspindle Fizzlegear","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.2,"y":29.2,"n":"Tinkmaster Overspark","e":1}],"cats":["engineering"]},"6032":{"id":6032,"t":"Sacred Cloth","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 2 Mooncloth to Meilosh in Timbermaw Hold.\n2 Mooncloth","desc":"Although the people of Timbermaw delight in the feel of runecloth, it is not sacred to us. But mooncloth is sacred.\nBring me a small supply of this holy cloth, and I will teach you a secret fashioning technique.","rew":"You will learn: Mooncloth Boots\nExperience: 5,650\n+100 reputation with Timbermaw Hold","back":"Have you brought the mooncloth, ‹name›?","done":"Ah, very good. This mooncloth will be used for garments sacred to our people. Thank you, ‹name›. Now I will train you.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":65.7,"y":2.8,"n":"Meilosh","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"4112":{"id":4112,"t":"Salve via Disenchanting","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Lesser Nether Essence","rew":"You will receive:\n2 Cenarion Plant Salve","back":"The power of a disenchanted magical item is felt by the essence it creates. I've devised a way to turn raw essence used by enchanters into a suitable reagent for creating Cenarion plant salve. You don't need a Cenarion beacon for this; any suitably disenchanted item that yields lesser nether essences will work.\nI just need a single lesser nether essence; in exchange, I will give you Cenarion plant salves. The essence is extremely potent - a little definitely goes a long way!","done":"Here are some Cenarion plant salves - I only need one lesser nether essence for this, ‹name›. Essence is by far the most potent item I can make use of to turn swords into plowshares, as it were. If you need more salve, then find me here!","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":46.7,"y":83.1,"n":"Maybess Riverbreeze","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"3792":{"id":3792,"t":"Morrowgrain to Feathermoon Stronghold","lv":55,"min":47,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"5 Morrowgrain","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Packet of Tharlendris Seeds\nExperience: 550\n+25 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Hello again, ‹name›. My research is progressing fairly well, but if you have five more Morrowgrain I'd be happy to take them off your hands. Well... happy is a figurative term in this case; the more I am around them, the more uncomfortable I feel. Still, my research demands I buckle down and get through this.","done":"Thanks ‹name›; I'll just store these out of the way for the time being. While I don't command the resources that Staghelm does, I am able to give you a little something for your trouble. Anyway, who knows what will happen if Staghelm keeps getting Morrowgrain after Morrowgrain. There's something fishy going on, mark my words.\nRemember that I'm always looking for more Morrowgrain. I'll take them in quantities of five at a time.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":32.4,"y":43.8,"n":"Quintis Jonespyre","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"7632":{"id":7632,"t":"The Ancient Leaf","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the owner of the Ancient Petrified Leaf. Good luck, ‹name›; It's a big world.\nAncient Petrified Leaf Cache of the Firelord 50 %\nProvided: Ancient Petrified Leaf","desc":"The epidermis of the leaf glows a bright green. The surface is extremely rugose, exposing several veins and wrinkles.\nIf you had to take a guess, you would say this leaf came from something ancient and powerful.\nMaybe you should find the original owner of this leaf?","rew":"Experience: 9,950","back":"<Vartrus groans.>","done":"Of course I recognize my own leaves. Look at that! It's in perfect condition.\nHow good of you to return it, ‹class›.\nPerhaps you could be of service to us and we to you.\nStart an item: Ancient Petrified Leaf End Vartrus the Ancient Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Class Hunter Shareable No Quest ID 7632\nThe chain\n4 quests at level 60, 19,900 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] The Ancient Leaf this quest\nFind the owner of the Ancient Petrified Leaf.\nAncient Petrified Leaf\n9,950 XP\n2 [ 60 ] One quest for each class\nHunter , Hunter , Hunter\nHastat the Ancient\n9,950 XP","cats":["hunter"]},"4512":{"id":4512,"t":"A Little Slime Goes a Long Way","lv":52,"min":48,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 6 Filled Cursed Ooze Jars and 6 Filled Tainted Ooze Jars to Laris Geardawdle in Ironforge.\n6 Filled Cursed Ooze Jar\n6 Filled Tainted Ooze Jar\nProvided: Package of Empty Ooze Containers","desc":"But the thing I've studied most is ooze. I know it sounds odd, but they're all over!\nI helped a lady in Menethil find her bag not too long ago--it was eaten by oozes. I've seen members of the Royal Apothecary Society from Undercity collecting samples of the stuff. I want to know why! Where does it come from?\nI've heard of more in Felwood. What I need are samples of the oozes there so I can further my research. I'll give you containers, you use them to collect a sample from the deceased creatures.","rew":"Money: 75 0 gold, 75 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,350\n+150 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Some of the experiments I've done are fascinating. I think with a little more work, I'll be able to figure out the nature of these creatures and how they play into how life developed on Azeroth... if they even have anything to do with it to begin with.\nOne of my biggest theories that isn't well liked is the idea that oozes and slimes are tied to the creation of this planet... almost like they're a secretion of it.\nBut I can't prove or disprove it until I get more samples.","done":"Amazing results, ‹name›! You got close enough to take a sample of the corrupted things, and managed to look no worse for wear! Thank you. Oh, these samples will be perfect. I can't wait to start testing on them.\nIf I'm right, I could be one of the Explorers' Leagues greatest scientists!\nThat'll prove to all the dwarves that it wasn't a mistake to allow us gnomes into Ironforge after the Gnomeregan incident.\nDun Morogh Felwood","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63.2,"y":24.8,"n":"Laris Geardawdle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"8912":{"id":8912,"t":"An Earnest Proposition","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -20g instead of 0.","obj":"Acquire 15 Winterspring Blood Samples and 20 gold and bring them along with a set of Bracers of Valor to Deliana in Ironforge.\n15 Winterspring Blood Sample Rabid Shardtooth 30 % , Elder Shardtooth 30 % , Shardtooth Bear 30 % , Shardtooth Mauler 30 % and 4 more\nBracers of Valor Blackhand Iron Guard 6.7 % , Smolderthorn Axe Thrower 4.5 % , Firebrand Legionnaire 3.5 % , Bloodaxe Warmonger 2.4 % and 2 more","desc":"Well met, ‹class›. I've something that might interest you.\nI have in my possession a set of armor much like the one worn by those of your profession, but of much higher quality. I'd be willing to trade the bracers for ordinary ones in exchange for a small favor.\nThe blood of the frostsabers and bears that inhabit Winterspring has properties I'm in need of at the moment. Bring me a sizeable sample of it along with the bracers and a small amount of gold. You shall find the effort worth your while.","rew":"You will receive:\nBracers of Heroism\nExperience: 6,600","back":"Have you brought me what I requested of you, ‹name›?","done":"Excellent! Let's perform the trade then. It's hard to part with this excellent armor, but I'm afraid I won't be needing it any time soon.\nIf you're interested in performing more work for me, I might be willing to give up the rest of the pieces.\nDun Morogh Winterspring","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"912":{"id":912,"t":"Stonesplinter trogg disguise","lv":12,"min":10,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","rew":"You will receive:\nKnowledge: Stonesplinter Disguise\nExperience: 230\nLevel 12 , requires level 10 Difficulty 10 15 18 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 912","cats":["loch-modan"]},"8672":{"id":8672,"t":"Stonespire the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"Your spirit burns with life, young ‹class›. I accept the homage you pay, and offer in return this token...","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":61.5,"y":37.8,"n":"Elder Stonespire","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"1952":{"id":1952,"t":"Mage's Wand","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Tabetha after her ritual.","desc":"I'll go make the wands now.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nIcefury Wand Nether Force Wand Ragefire Wand\nExperience: 3,150","done":"Here are the wands I made. Take your pick!","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":46.1,"y":57.1,"n":"Tabetha","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"752":{"id":752,"t":"A Humble Task","lv":2,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 0 instead of 17c. New rewards: Mining for Dummies, Wild Harvest, Pelt Collecting for Beginners.","obj":"Chief Hawkwind wants you to search for his mother near the water well to the southeast of Camp Narache.","desc":"All members of the tribe share in the harmony of life. We live together and work together.\nOur commitment to one another carries with it a high degree of responsibility. I ask of you now a humble task.\nMy mother set out this morning to fetch water from the well to the southeast of Narache. It has been quite some time now. Perhaps you could check on her for me while I attend to tribal matters here?","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMining for Dummies Wild Harvest Pelt Collecting for Beginners\nNew in Forever: Mining for Dummies, Wild Harvest, Pelt Collecting for Beginners.\nExperience: 85\n+50 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"You traveled all this way just to help an old woman? My my, aren't you a keeper?","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":43.9,"y":76.7,"n":"Chief Hawkwind","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":48.8,"y":80.9,"n":"Greatmother Hawkwind","e":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9072":{"id":9072,"t":"Earthshatter Boots","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Rimblat Earthshatter at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Earthshatter Boots if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Boots, 12 Wartorn Chain Scraps, 1 Arcanite Bar and 3 Nexus Crystals.\nDesecrated Boots Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Gothik the Harvester 0 % in Naxxramas , Instructor Razuvious 0 % in Naxxramas\n12 Wartorn Chain Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 14.4 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 13.5 % in Naxxramas , Spirit of Naxxramas 13.3 % in Naxxramas , Living Monstrosity 12.5 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\nArcanite Bar\n3 Nexus Crystal","desc":"Would you honor me by returning the armor of those that fell in the defense of these lands?\nThe armor has been desecrated and is undoubtedly being used for evil; however, with wartorn armor scraps, the desecrated armor can be renewed and worn for battle once more.\nBring me the remnants of the fallen along with purification materials and Earthshatter shall be yours to don.\nSearch Naxxramas.","rew":"You will receive:\nEarthshatter Boots\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Earthshatter Boots.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.3,"y":49.4,"n":"Rimblat Earthshatter","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"9232":{"id":9232,"t":"The Only Song I Know...","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -30g instead of 0.","obj":"Craftsman Wilhelm at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants you to bring him 2 Frozen Runes, 2 Essence of Water, 2 Blue Sapphires and 30 gold pieces.\n2 Frozen Rune Frozen Rune in Naxxramas\n2 Essence of Water Princess Tempestria 70.6 % , Lord Skwol 53.3 % , Hydrospawn 11 % , Toxic Horror 7.2 % and 4 more\n2 Blue Sapphire Alzzin's Minion 2.5 % , Rich Thorium Vein 0.8 % , Ooze Covered Rich Thorium Vein 0.8 % , Small Thorium Vein 0.7 % and 4 more","desc":"You fancy yourself a hero of the Dawn, eh? I've seen our greatest soldiers get rolled over by Kel'Thuzad's plebes! How well could someone so clueless possibly fare in Naxxramas?\n<Wilhelm sighs.>\nBah, what choice do I got? You're the best I can do; I may as well help you.\nOmarion left me with one recipe. It's the only song I know... I can make a few variations of these pants; you just gotta supply the materials.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGlacial Leggings Icebane Leggings Icy Scale Leggings Polar Leggings\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You haven't run into Omarion, have you?","done":"<Wilhelm wipes the sweat from his brow.>\nThat's some hard work! Enjoy the pants, ‹class›. At least you'll die in a clean pair now.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.2,"y":49.9,"n":"Craftsman Wilhelm","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"5632":{"id":5632,"t":"Returning Home","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Priestess Alathea in Darnassus.","desc":"Oh, yes, of course. Hello, ‹name›. A messenger from our order was here not too long ago looking for you. She mentioned something important happening back in Darnassus and that you should return to the Temple of the Moon as soon as you can. When you arrive, speak to Priestess Alathea. I believe it has something to do with your progressing so well in our ways.\nAgain, return to Darnassus when you can.","rew":"You will learn: Starshards\nExperience: 210","done":"Wonderful, you've returned home, ‹name›. It always pleases Tyrande and myself when those we've trained go out into the world and return to us safely. How have things been with you? Does Elune still bless your travels? Perhaps after we speak more about the business at hand, you could tell me more of your travels.\nStormwind City Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":35.7,"y":63.2,"n":"Nara Meideros","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":39.5,"y":81.2,"n":"Priestess Alathea","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"8832":{"id":8832,"t":"One Commendation Signet","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Horde Commendation Signet","back":"For those adventurers who have but a single commendation signet, I'll exchange it for a small amount of recognition with the Undercity.\nPlease bear in mind that it is better to hand over a stack of ten signets at once; your efforts will receive greater recognition in doing so. We offer a single signet exchange as a service for those who don't have enough for a full stack of ten.\nWith that being said, I stand ready to assist you if you still wish to hand in a single signet.","done":"Very well - your deeds have been entered into the records, and you are duly recognized for your efforts. Keep up the good work, ‹class›.\nIf you have any more signets to hand in, then I am able to assist you further in that regard.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":42.5,"y":38.7,"n":"Officer Redblade","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["reputation"]},"8992":{"id":8992,"t":"The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Brazier of Beckoning to summon forth the spirit of Kormok and slay him. Return to Bodley inside Blackrock Mountain with the recombined Lord Valthalak's Amulet and the Brazier of Beckoning.\nLord Valthalak's Amulet\nBrazier of Beckoning\nKormok slain\nProvided: Brazier of Beckoning","desc":"Now we have what we need, so it's time to discuss who it is that you'll be summoning next.\nKormok was ok for an ogre, right up until he turned to necromancy. After that, things got creepy for just about everyone in the outfit. It was no surprise then when he took his piece of the amulet and returned to his new home, Scholomance.\nBut even there, or perhaps especially there, he was not safe from the spectral assassins. They slew him right in front of his master, Ras Frostwhisper.","rew":"Experience: 8,300","back":"I commend you, ‹name›, if you have returned with the completed amulet. If not, however, please take care of that as there is no time to waste, I assure you!","done":"Good work, ‹name›! Kormok wasn't all that bad for an ogre, at least not while he was still alive, so I hope he gets the rest that he deserves. And now we have the completed amulet! But we still have the hardest test ahead of us.\nIn order for the brazier to be attuned to calling forth Lord Valthalak, there are a few more items that need to be gathered and brought back to me here.","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":32.3,"y":25.8,"n":"Bodley","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["scholomance"]},"93072":{"id":93072,"t":"Long term solutions","lv":43,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Maintain your reputation with the Magram clan and slay 2 Outcast Scouts, 6 Outcast Marauders, and 8 Outcast Necromancers then return to Hagiak at the Magram Front.\nOutcast Scout slain : 0/ 2\nOutcast Marauder slain : 0/ 6\nOutcast Necromancer slain : 0/ 8","desc":"There is a second centaur village out here, to the southwest. That one belongs to the Gelkis. You expect me to send you over just to spill some blood, right? Good. That had best be your first thought, else I would cast doubt on your allegiance to the Magram!\nWhat are you waiting for? Go! Kill!","rew":"Money: 30 0 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,600\n+500 reputation with Magram Clan Centaur\n0 reputation with Gelkis Clan Centaur\nShen'dralas Desolace\nShen'dralas Open the zone on the world map Level 43 , requires level 35 Difficulty 35 39 41 46 54 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 93072\nThe chain\n15 quests from level 32 to 43, 36,630 XP in all.\n1 [ 35 ] Brutal Politics\nGain a Friendly reputation with the Magram, then speak with Warug.\nCaptain Pentigast Desolace\n2,050 XP\n2 [ 32 ] Assault on the Kolkar\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram.\nWarug Desolace\n2,550 XP\n[ 33 ] Magram Alliance\nGain a Friendly reputation with the Magram, then speak with Warug.\nGurda Wildmane Desolace\n650 XP\n3 [ 33 ] Broken Tears\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 3 Broken Tears to Warug in the Magram Village.\nWarug Desolace\n2,650 XP\n4 [ 40 ] A Conqueror's Crown\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and return a Conqueror's Crown from the Badlands to Warug in Magram Village.\n3,150 XP\n5 [ 40 ] Valley of Bones\nImprove your reputation with the Magram, and locate Orgrul near the Valley of Bones south of Magram Village.\n320 XP\n6 [ 42 ] Mountain of Bones\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 426 Gently Cursed Bones to Orgrul south of the Magram Village in Desolace.\n3,450 XP\n7 [ 42 ] Corrupting Tears\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 3 Petrified Bark and 3 Imbued Tears back to Orgrul.\n3,450 XP\n8 [ 41 ] Proof of Concept\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, then bring 426 Well Cursed Bones from a successful ritual back to Orgrul.\n2,450 XP\n9 [ 40 ] Bone Raising\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, and use the Enhanced Necromancy Staff to fully raise undead that are struggling to emerge throughout the Valley of Bones.\n2,350 XP\n[ 42 ] No Mercy for the Weak\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, and slay 5 Gelkis Captives scattered around the Valley of Bones.\n2,550 XP\n10 [ 43 ] Bristleback Retreat\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and slay quilboar at Bristleback Retreat.\n3,600 XP\n11 [ 43 ] Long-Term Solutions this quest\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram clan and slay 2 Outcast Scouts, 6 Out","cats":["shendralas"]},"8352":{"id":8352,"t":"Scepter of the Council","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 9,950 experience instead of 10,634, 0.94 times as much.","obj":"Bring an Abyssal Scepter to Bor Wildmane in Cenarion Hold.\nAbyssal Scepter Prince Skaldrenox , High Marshal Whirlaxis , Baron Kazum , Lord Skwol","desc":"Huum and I were just talking about you. He tells me you're just about ready to try your hand at fighting an Abyssal Lord!\nI must tell you this is a very dangerous endeavor. You'd better bring backup. And I don't mean one or two of your friends, I'm talking about a top-notch, battle-ready fighting force. If your friends are as good as you, you might even defeat it!\nIf you do - and I'll want evidence, as always - I'll give you a truly great reward.","rew":"You will receive:\nChest of Spoils\nMoney: 2 70 2 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Well, how did it go? I'd do anything to leave my post and wrestle one of those things myself!","done":"You... you did it! You did it, ‹name›! Here! Take this. It's the biggest chest we had lying around and I filled it with some of the best stuff we found.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":48.6,"y":37.8,"n":"Bor Wildmane","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"79952":{"id":79952,"t":"Rwlrwlrwlrwl","lv":35,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"RwlRwlRwlRwl!","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 280","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nRwlRwlRwlRwl! (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.8,"y":80.2,"n":"Garion Wendell","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.6,"y":33,"n":"Owen Thadd","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"81952":{"id":81952,"t":"Everyday etiquette","lv":45,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Everyday Etiquette","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 6 0 gold, 6 silver, 0 copper Experience: 390","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nEveryday Etiquette (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.8,"y":80.2,"n":"Garion Wendell","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.6,"y":33,"n":"Owen Thadd","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"1072":{"id":1072,"t":"An Old Colleague","lv":21,"min":17,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Lomac Gearstrip in Ironforge.","desc":"The device I'm thinking about is my most advanced version to date. But we'll need a special potion if it's to work. I'm thinking we might as well get the good stuff since this mission could be your last.\nAnd for that, we're going to need some potent explosives: Nitromirglyceronium.\nThe only person who can make NG-5 is an old friend of mine: Lomac Gearstrip. Look for him in Tinker Town.\nYou talk him into making us some NG-5, I'll get to work on placement for my devices.","rew":"Experience: 825\n+50 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","done":"Ahhh. Gaxim sent you, huh? How do I know you're not lying to me?! Hmm? Hmm?\nStonetalon Mountains Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":59.5,"y":67.1,"n":"Gaxim Rustfizzle","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.7,"y":29.4,"n":"Lomac Gearstrip","e":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"192":{"id":192,"t":"Panther Mastery","lv":38,"min":28,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Sir S. J. Erlgadin of Nesingwary's Expedition wants you to kill 10 Shadowmaw Panthers.\nShadowmaw Panther slain : 0/ 10","desc":"Now the hard part. A true panther hunter can show skill by dropping Shadowmaw Panthers, the deadliest in Stranglethorn. Prove to us that you can slay 10 of these beasts.\nIf you think they are hard to track, wait until you attempt to slay one....","rew":"Experience: 2,150","back":"What are you doing here, ‹name›! You should be crawling through the brush, trying to kill 10 Shadowmaw Panthers. I thought you fancied yourself a big game hunter?","done":"You've done well, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":35.6,"y":10.5,"n":"Sir S. J. Erlgadin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"592":{"id":592,"t":"Saving Yenniku","lv":46,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Filled Soul Gem to Nimboya.\nFilled Soul Gem\nProvided: Soul Gem","desc":"I have reshaped the Mind's Eye into a Soul Gem. Its purpose is twofold: you must use it to stun Yenniku, and once stunned place it upon his head to entrap his soul.\nThen, bring the gem to Nimboya.\nYenniku dwells with Zanzil the Outcast, at the Ruins of Aboraz, along the Crystal Shore on the distant Cape of Stranglethorn.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nNimboya's Mystical Staff Medal of Courage\nExperience: 5,050\n+150 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"‹name›. Kin'weelay told me you set out to capture Yenniku.\nIs it true? Do you have him?","done":"You've done it! You freed Yenniku from the will of Zanzil, and completed the mission I had thought was so desperate.\nOur tribe will remember your name in songs, ‹name›, and we will etch your tale in stone so that it will live forever.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":32.3,"y":27.7,"n":"Kin'weelay","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":32.2,"y":27.7,"n":"Nimboya","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"1392":{"id":1392,"t":"Noboru the Cudgel","lv":39,"min":29,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Noboru's Cudgel to the leader of The Harborage in the Swamp of Sorrows.\nNoboru's Cudgel Noboru the Cudgel\nProvided: Noboru's Cudgel","desc":"Noboru has plagued the Draenei of the Harborage for months, and his cudgel is a symbol of the brutality they have suffered at the hands of the lost ones.","rew":"Experience: 2,250","back":"Greetings. And welcome to the Harborage.","done":"You have gained the weapon of the dreaded Noboru? Is he then dead?\nThis is a joyous day for the Harborage. Noboru and his gang were a terror to us, wandering the swamps and killing any Draenei who crossed his path. He was a direct threat to our survival, and we did not have the strength to face him.\nWe are fortunate to have a friend in you, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":26,"y":31.4,"n":"Magtoor","e":1}],"cats":["swamp-of-sorrows"]},"992":{"id":992,"t":"Gadgetzan Water Survey","lv":46,"min":38,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the untapped dowsing widget near the pool of water by Sandsorrow Watch. Once you have collected the sample, return the tapped dowsing widget to Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser in Gadgetzan.\nTapped Dowsing Widget\nProvided: Untapped Dowsing Widget","desc":"We've got a position open for a temporary junior-grade surveyor in the Gadgetzan Water Company, if you're interested!\nWith the nomads seizing all our wells, we need to exploit more free sources of water! There is water to be had in the desert, but only to those smart enough to survey them first.\nTake this dowsing widget and tap a sample of the water by the pool near Sandsorrow Watch. It's right in sight of the trolls around there. Bring the tapped widget back to me when you're done!","rew":"Money: 35 0 gold, 35 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,050\n+75 reputation with Gadgetzan","back":"Welcome back, Junior Surveyor ‹name›! Have you completed your assignment yet?","done":"What's this? You were ambushed by some sort of bad mojo creepy-crawly? Oh, this does not bode well for the Gadgetzan Water Company, no indeed...\nI guess I should have told you about the reports coming in on some crazy bug-creatures that appear to be sucking up all the water in the desert. At first, I thought it was just a crock. We have enough trouble with the nomads as is; I thought it was just more of their shenanigans. Well, now we know at least!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":50.2,"y":27.5,"n":"Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"32":{"id":32,"t":"Rise of the Silithid","lv":48,"min":39,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the report to Zilzibin Drumlore in Orgrimmar.\nInsect Analysis Report\nProvided: Insect Analysis Report","desc":"Here's your report. I urge you to take it to someone who might have working knowledge in this kind of thing.\nI know this troll scholar named Zilzibin Drumlore. He's spent a lot of time studying life forms that are unique to the ecology of Azeroth; he's a historian to boot! If you want someone to help figure out what exactly this threat is and how to stop it, give this report to him. We're going to need all the help we can get.\nZil lives in a house on the second tier of the Drag in Orgrimmar.","rew":"Experience: 5,450\n+150 reputation with Gadgetzan\n+150 reputation with Horde","back":"I'm sorry. I don't know you... but from the look of things you have at least heard something of me. Now, what can I help you with? Do you have something for me?","done":"This report... I've dealt with these beasts before. Fizzledowser was wise to send this. and you, to me.\nThese creatures will consume the Tanaris desert rapidly; they are nothing short of one of the greatest menaces we all will ever face. Familiarize yourself with this name, ‹name›: silithid. The insects mentioned here are the silithid, and they are the tools of one of the greatest threats that both the Horde and Alliance face.\nIf only we were smart enough to see that before.\nTanaris Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":50.2,"y":27.5,"n":"Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":56.3,"y":46.7,"n":"Zilzibin Drumlore","e":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"8752":{"id":8752,"t":"The Path of the Conqueror","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nSignet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","done":"Impressive, little one. You have gone through much trouble to gain the favor of the Bronze Flight. Your dedication is noted.\nThe signet ring of the conqueror will greatly enhance your physical attacks.\nBe warned, once you have chosen your path, you will have no recourse should you change your mind.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.3,"y":50,"n":"Anachronos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"2992":{"id":2992,"t":"The Divination","lv":47,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Wait until Grimshade performs the ritual of divination.","desc":"Give me room while I perform a ritual of divination. I will find the connection between the feather you brought me and its owner, and follow that connection to Sharpbeak himself.\nThat is... I will if all goes according to plan. If it does not, then... you better close your eyes.","rew":"Experience: 1,050\n+25 reputation with Wildhammer Clan\n+25 reputation with Ironforge","done":"The ritual was a success. I have seen Sharpbeak and can tell you how to find him.","pins":[{"z":"Blasted Lands","x":66.9,"y":19.5,"n":"Thadius Grimshade","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"1152":{"id":1152,"t":"Test of Lore","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Braug Dimspirit near the entrance to Talondeep Path in Stonetalon Mountains.","desc":"Your time with me is just about finished. I am knowledgeable, but the Test of Lore is not mine to give. There are lessons to be learned and places to visit that others claim domain over.\nIf you are prepared, then seek out Braug Dimspirit--he is a shaman of great wisdom. He will test you further, so heed his words, ‹name›.\nWhen you are ready, find the tunnel that connects the Stonetalon Mountains with Ashenvale: Braug dwells near there. And be careful, ‹name›, the night elves may wish to impede your test.","rew":"Experience: 1,200\n+50 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"The days and nights grow colder throughout the world as goblins rape the land, and the night elves point fingers at the younger races. The Forsaken and orcs are not the only ones to blame for the hardships found throughout Kalimdor and Lordaeron. Many of the intelligent races have contributed to the world's pain. Dorn knows this, and he has sent you to me because you have shown the attributes necessary to realize it also.\nNow you stand before Braug.\nThousand Needles Stonetalon Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":53.9,"y":41.5,"n":"Dorn Plainstalker","s":1},{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":78.8,"y":45.7,"n":"Braug Dimspirit","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"99152":{"id":99152,"t":"As above so below","lv":10,"min":7,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 6 Faintly Glowing Bones for Hilda the Breaker.\n6 Faintly Glowing Bone","desc":"While the Tarnished in Shadowvale to the southwest are definitely a problem, we cannot allow the cellars below the town to fester into a full-blown Scourge uprising on Bandarion Keep.\nI need to get these trainees up to snuff in case that happens. You, however, are going to receive what I like to call a crash course.\nTravel beneath Shadowvale and retrieve some of their wretched bones so we can study them further. I need ones that still retain some of the initial reanimation magic--that's glowing ones.","back":"You'd best not be returning empty-handed. I either need the bones I asked for, or your body on a stretcher to confirm you at least gave it your all trying to get them.","done":"Well done, recruit. We might just make something out of you yet.\nWith these bones we may be able to better understand how such a threat was able to go unnoticed for so long.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":22,"y":47.2,"n":"Hilda the Breaker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"1472":{"id":1472,"t":"Devourer of Souls","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Godrick Farsan in the Temple of the Damned.","desc":"A succubus is a devourer of souls, destroyer of hearts, tempter of men. A creature of profound evil and of singular mind.\nIt cannot be brought into our world without a stimulus.\nThus we use its own strength against it. With the hearts of good men, pure men, loving men, the succubus will be unable to resist, and will cross into our world. Then you can dominate it, and make it your own.\nSpeak with my assistant, Godrick Farsan, within the Temple. He will help you find your bait.","rew":"Experience: 160","done":"You were sent by Carendin? ‹name›, then.\nDo not think light of me because my sight is gone. I see things that lie behind now, with clarity I had never known. What I once thought a curse, is now a boon.","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":85.1,"y":26,"n":"Carendin Halgar","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":84.8,"y":14.8,"n":"Godrick Farsan","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1712":{"id":1712,"t":"Cyclonian","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the items on Bath'rah's Parchment to Bath'rah the Windwatcher in Alterac.\n8 Liferoot Liferoot in Scarlet Monastery , Weegli Blastfuse 66.7 % in Zul'Farrak , Zaruk 61.9 % , Tor'gan 11.9 % and 4 more\n30 Bloodscalp Tusk Bloodscalp Scavenger 37 % , Bloodscalp Mystic 37 % , Bloodscalp Beastmaster 37 % , Bloodscalp Shaman 37 % and 4 more\nEssence of the Exile\nProvided: Bath'rah's Parchment","desc":"I have spent ages watching this site. I watch, so that one day I might see the great Cyclonian fall. But I have not yet found a champion to defeat the wind lord.\nPerhaps you are that champion.\nProve it to me. Gather the items I need to summon Cyclonian, and I will know you are a great warrior. Perhaps then you can defeat him and gain his whirlwind heart.\nIf so, then I will infuse the heart's power in a weapon, and I will give that weapon to you.\nHere is a parchment with the items I need.","rew":"Experience: 2,350","back":"Do you have the items, ‹name›? Gathering them is the proof I need that you have the strength to face Cyclonian.","done":"You have gathered the items for my spell, and have shown me your strength and cunning. But the next stage of our quest is even more perilous.\nLet us hope your strength does not falter.","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":80.5,"y":66.9,"n":"Bath'rah the Windwatcher","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"1792":{"id":1792,"t":"Whirlwind Weapon","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nWhirlwind Axe Whirlwind Sword Whirlwind Warhammer\nExperience: 3,900","done":"I have the whirlwind heart, and am ready to place it within your vessel of choice.\nChoose your weapon, ‹name›, and know that its power is the power of Cyclonian.","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":80.5,"y":66.9,"n":"Bath'rah the Windwatcher","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"8432":{"id":8432,"t":"Battle of Warsong Gulch","lv":39,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Warsong Marks of Honor to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"The battle in Warsong Gulch against the Silverwing Sentinels is of great importance. Under the guise of protecting a forest that doesn't belong to them, the Alliance seeks to deny the Horde one of our largest sources for lumber.\nDo not let this happen, ‹name›! Come back to me with proof of serving the Horde in a worthy manner!","rew":"Experience: 1,500\n+50 reputation with Warsong Outriders","back":"The battle in Warsong Gulch against the Silverwing Sentinels is of great importance. Under the guise of protecting a forest that doesn't belong to them, the Alliance seeks to deny the Horde one of our largest sources for lumber.\nDo not let this happen, ‹name›! Come back to me with proof of serving the Horde in a worthy manner!","done":"Excellent! You've shown your worth by defending our operations in Warsong Gulch! May word of your honor spread far and wide across our lands.\nThe Barrens Arathi Highlands Undercity","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.7,"y":8.7,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.5,"y":29.1,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":58.3,"y":97.9,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"7872":{"id":7872,"t":"Vanquish the Invaders!","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 3,900 experience instead of 5,500, 0.71 times as much.","obj":"Enter Warsong Gulch and defeat the Horde, obtain a Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor, and return to Sentinel Farsong at the Silverwing Grove.\nWarsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"Beyond this tunnel you will find a field of strife and turmoil, young ‹class›. The Horde continue to decimate our sacred forest, cutting down the evergreen foliage to power their machines of war.\nEnter Warsong Gulch and defend Silverwing Hold. Push back the invading Horde forces!\nDo this, and earn a talisman of merit. Bring me such a talisman, ‹name›, and I shall reward you.","rew":"Money: 1 95 1 gold, 95 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,900\n+200 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels\n+200 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels\n+200 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels\n+200 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels\nLevel 45 , requires level 40 Difficulty 40 41 43 48 57 Side Human, Dwarf, Night Elf, Gnome Type PvP Shareable No Repeatable Yes Quest ID 7872","cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"5232":{"id":5232,"t":"Return to the Bulwark","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Filled Dalson's Tears Bottle to Shadow Priestess Vandis at the Bulwark, Western Plaguelands.\nFilled Dalson's Tears Bottle\nProvided: Filled Dalson's Tears Bottle","desc":"You carefully fill the bottle with enough of the cauldron's ichors for what you consider to be suitably sized sample.\nWith the poison in hand, it is time to return to Shadow Priestess Vandis at the Bulwark to complete the mission.","rew":"Money: 85 0 gold, 85 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,800\n+50 reputation with Undercity\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"We know that each cauldron employs a different mix of reagents to generate its plague-inducing toxin; likewise, we know that we will need to develop a counter agent that is unique for each cauldron. Your sample from Dalson's Tears will be the key to figure out that cauldron's distinct reagent requirement.","done":"Ah, there is plenty in here for study. Well done, ‹name›!\nFor now, the next step is in our hands. We'll need to produce a list of reagents that, when combined with what is already in the cauldron, will act as its counter.\nThe only way we will be able to introduce this is by placing the reagents into the cauldron directly. Apothecary Dithers will have more information on that, so be sure to speak with him as soon as possible.\nWestern Plaguelands Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":46.2,"y":51.9,"n":"Scourge Cauldron","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83,"y":71.9,"n":"Shadow Priestess Vandis","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"92752":{"id":92752,"t":"Explosive consultation","lv":16,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Return to Alba Fairmoon in Westfall.\nProvided: Extra-Destructive Explosives","desc":"That's it - the bomb's ready to go! Careful with that detonator, now.","rew":"Money: 4 0 gold, 4 silver, 0 copper Experience: 575\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","done":"I'm glad you've returned, Busch.\nStormwind City Westfall","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":54.6,"y":8,"n":"Sprite Jumpsprocket","s":1},{"z":"Westfall","x":52.4,"y":53,"n":"Alba Fairmoon","e":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"93552":{"id":93552,"t":"Harvesting windstones","lv":4,"min":2,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 15 Windstone Clusters from Raw Windstones in Thendal Grove.\n15 Windstone Cluster","desc":"Windstones are a critical resource on Zephras Isle as they contain the raw, concentrated energy of the winds themselves. The wind elementals who used to live here on zephras with us vanished several centuries ago, and since then, the magic that sustains this island is slowly fading. Not without limitations, the Windstones are still a reliable energy source, and are incredibly valuable to us.\nYou'll find raw Windstones scattered around the grove, think you can help me harvest them?","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMining for Dummies Wild Harvest Pelt Collecting for Beginners\nYou will also receive:\n3 Windstone\nMoney: 75 0 gold, 0 silver, 75 copper Experience: 360\n+50 reputation with Windshapers\n+50 reputation with High Order","back":"Hello there, ‹class›.","done":"Thank you very much for these. As elves we all have a deep connection to magic and these windstones are becoming more and more precious as the magic imbued into this island by the great anchor pylons continues to fade.\nwindstones aren't the only beneficial thing you can harvest from the land. Please, take one of these manuals.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":43.2,"y":24,"n":"Dalia the Collector","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"98512":{"id":98512,"t":"Alaketh assassins","lv":11,"min":6,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Kill 10 Al'Aketh Assassins in the Shen'dar Highlands.\nAl'Aketh Assassin slain : 0/ 10","desc":"You there, stranger. Get low and keep quiet. We are not alone here.\nI was on patrol near the border and noticed that there are a number of Al'Aketh skulking around the house just up the hill there to the north. I don't know what they are doing here, but it can't be good.\nIf you want to make yourself useful, get in there and take them out. I'll wait here and watch your back.","back":"I wonder what they are after?","done":"I'm glad you made it back. That group of Al'Aketh looked like stone cold killers.\nThank you for your aid, I'll include your assistance in my report when I return to Valanaar.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":56.8,"y":61,"n":"Fendaal Windstone","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"8192":{"id":8192,"t":"Animist's Caress","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring me thise things and I will create a powerful enchantment for you!\nPrimal Hakkari Idol\nPunctured Voodoo Doll\nPrimal Hakkari Idol Jin'do the Hexxer in Zul'Gurub , Bloodlord Mandokir in Zul'Gurub\nPunctured Voodoo Doll Voodoo Slave 0.1 % in Zul'Gurub , Hakkari Shadowcaster 0.1 % in Zul'Gurub , Gurubashi Axe Thrower 0 % in Zul'Gurub , Gurubashi Headhunter 0 % in Zul'Gurub and 4 more","desc":"Zanza can create the ancient troll enchantments with the right components. The first is a primal Hakkari idol that must be taken from the most powerful of the Hakkari lieutenants: Jin'do and the Bloodlord.\nThe second is a punctured voodoo doll. These can be found in the piles of refuse that litter this foul place. Look inside the jinxed hoodoo.\nBring me these things and I will create a powerful enchantment for you!","rew":"You will receive:\nAnimist's Caress\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Bring me these things and I will create a powerful enchantment for you!","done":"Use it well ‹class›. Show the Hakkari no mercy!\nStart Zanza the Restless Zul'Gurub End Zanza the Restless Zul'Gurub Level 60 , requires level 58 Difficulty 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Raid Shareable No Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8192","cats":["zulgurub"]},"8112":{"id":8112,"t":"Enchanted South Seas Kelp","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","obj":"Enchanted South Seas Kelp","rew":"You will receive:\nEnchanted South Seas Kelp\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"How be that talisman, mon? It look like it be time to add a little more magic and mojo to its leaves. It need a little bloom in its wilt. Give it here and Maywiki fix it right up.","done":"Now you take the evil trolls in Zul'Gurub and show them what your nature powers can do, mon!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":16,"n":"Maywiki of Zuldazar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]}});